Add, edit, list, remove, export and import lifecycle rules

Usage:
  nexoctl ilm rule [flags]
  nexoctl ilm rule [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Add a lifecycle rule to a bucket
  edit        Change a lifecycle rule of a bucket
  export      Print the lifecycle configuration of a bucket (JSON or S3 XML)
  import      Replace the lifecycle configuration of a bucket (JSON or S3 XML)
  list        List the lifecycle rules of a bucket
  remove      Remove lifecycle rules of a bucket

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for rule

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl ilm rule [command] --help" for more information about a command.
